    "rs|RS211_2007-08-14|floor": " \n \nTuesday  \n14 August, 2007  \n23 Sravana, 1929 (Saka) \nVol.211 \nNo. 3 \nPARLIAMENTARY DEBATES \nRAJYA SABHA \nOFFICIAL REPORT \nCONTENTS \nObituary Reference (page 1) \nOral answers to Questions (pages 2— 21) \nWritten Answers to Starred Questions (pages 21— 35) \nWritten Answers to Unstarred Questions (pages 35— 158) \nMinister Introduced (pages 159) \nPapers laid on the Table (pages 159— 166) \nReport of the Committee on Papers Laid on the Table - Presented \n(page 166) Report   of the* Department   Related   Parliamentary   \nStanding \nCommittee on Industry - Presented {page 166) Report of the Committee \non Empowerment of Women - Laid on the \nTable - (page 167) Recommendations   of  the   Business   Advisory   \nCommittee \n(pages 167—68) Matters raised with permission -Collapse of Chakki \nbridge on the National Highway No. 20 \n(pages 167—68) Grant of pension to Kerala's Freedom Fighters' of \n1946 Naval \nMutiny (page 169) Demand for construction of memorials in memory \nof the designer \nof National Flag (page 170) \n[P.T.O \n© \nRAJYA SABHA SECRETARIAT \n                                                 NEW DELHI         \n  PRICE : Rs. 50.00 \n\nMerciless beating of women in Jammu (pages 170— 72) \nDemand for action against Chief Minister and Deputy Home Minister of Gujarat (page \n172) \nDadasaheb Phalke Award to Shri Shyam Bengal (page 173) \nGovernment Bills - \nThe Private Universities (Establishment and Regulation) Bill, 1995 -  Withdrawn (page \n173) \nThe Constitution (Scheduled Castes) Order (Amendment) Bill, 2007 -  Passed {pages \n173—212)  \nShort Duration Discussion - \nHeavy floods in various parts of the country and the relief measures undertaken by the \nGovernment (pages 212— 21) \nStatement by Minister - \nStatus of implementation of Forty -Ninth Report of the Department -Related \nParliamentary Standing Committee on Finance(page 221) \nWeb-site Address   :   http://rajyasabha.nic.in \nhttp://parliamentofindi.nic.in \nE-mail Address       :   rsedit-e@sansad.nic.in \n\nRAJYA SABHA \nTuesday. the 14th August, 2007/23 Sravana, 1929 (Saka) \nThe House met at eleven of the clock, \nMR. CHAIRMAN in the Chair. \nOBITUARY REFERENCE \nMR. CHAIRMAN: Hon. Members, I refer with profound sorrow to the passing \naway of Shri Shankarrao Bajirao Bobdey, a former Member of this House on th e 8th \nJuly, 2007, at the age of 92. \nBorn in September, 1915, at Khamgaon in Buldana district of Maharashtra, Shri \nBobdey had his education at Fergusson College, Pune and Law College, Nagpur. \nAn advocate by profession, Shri Bobdey took keen interest in prom oting cooperative \nmovement in the country. He was associated with various social welfare, educational \nand cooperative organisations and served them in various capacities. Shri Bobdey \nstudied cooperative movements in Europe and visited  co-operative institutions in \nFrance, England, Germany, Switzerland, Italy and Holland. He also participated in the \nInternational Cooperative Conference at Paris as an Indian representative in the year \n1971. \nShri Bobdey represented the State of Maharashtra in this House for tw o consecutive \nterms from April, 1964 to April, 1970, and, again from April, 1970 to April, 1976. \nIn the passing away of Shri Shankarrao Bajirao Bobdey, the country has lost a \ndistinguished social worker and a veteran Parliamentarian. \nI request Members to r ise in their places and observe silence as a mark of respect to \nthe memory of the departed. \n(Hon. Members then stood in silence for one minute) \nMR. CHAIRMAN: Secretary -General will convey to the members of the bereaved \nfamily our deep sense of sorrow and sympathy. \n\n2 Oral answers [RAJYA SABHA] to Questions \nORAL ANSWERS TO QUESTIONS \nLeakages in domes of Jama Masjid, Delhi \n*41.SHRI AMIR ALAM KHAN: Will the Minister of CULTURE be pleased to \nstate: \n   (a) whether Government are aware that there are multiple leakages in the domes of \nthe 17th century old mosque Jama Masjid, Delhi; \n(b) whether Government have made any assessment of damage caused due to \nleakages; and \n(c) what is preventing Government to take immediate remedial measures to \nconserve the mosque inspite of allocation of funds? \nTHE MINISTER OF CULTURE (SHRIMATI AMBIKA SONI): (a) to (c) The \nStatement is laid on the Table of the House. \nStatement \n(a) to (c) Jama Masjid at Delhi is not a centrally protected monument. However, as \nper the directions of the Hon'ble High  Court of Delhi detailed condition assessment of \nthe monument including the domes has been carried out by the Delhi Wakf Board \nthrough a conservation architect. Based on this report, Archaeological Survey of India  \nhas sanctioned an estimate for Rs. 47.52 l akhs. The conservation works identified at the \nmonument include water tightening and resetting of the marble slabs of the domes to \narrest seepage. An amount of Rs. 10 lakhs has been allotted \nfor 2007-08 and the work is in progress. \n \nश्री  आ�मर  आलम खान  : सभाप ‍�त  महोदय , हमार�  पाट�  के  \nसभी  नेताओं  के  कल आपको  मुबारकबाद  पेश  क�  और आज सदन  क�  \nकायर्वाह�  का  आपका  पहला  �दन  है  ।  इत्तफाक  से  आज आपने  \nमुझे  पहला  प्रश्न  करने  का  मौका  �दया , इ स के  �लए  म�  आपका  \nधन्यवाद  अदा  करता  हूं  ।  सभाप�त  महोदय , माननीय  मंत्री  जी  \nने  अपने  जवाब  म�  �दल्ल�  का  जामा  मिस्जद  को  वक्क  बोडर्  \nके  अधीन  बताते  हुए  अपना  पल्ला  झाडन�  क�   को�शश  क�  है , \nजब�क  यह  राष्ट्र�य  धरोहर  क�  प्रतीक  है   ।  माननीय  मंत्री  \nजी  ने  पु\nरातत्व   �वभाग  से  45.52 लाख  रूपए  इ स के  रख-रखाव  \nहेतु  स्वीकार  भी  �कए  ह�  ।  म�  माननीय  मंत्री  जी  से  वह  \nजानना  चाहूंगा  �क  आप ऐसी  कोई  �न�ध , जैसे  राष्ट्र�य  \nसंस्कृ �त  �न�ध , आ�द  जामा  मिस्जद  के  रख-रखाव  व संर�ण  \nके  �लए  तय कर� गे , िजससे  हमारे  दे श  क�  यह  धरोहर  साल� -\nसाल  हमारे  दे श  क�  पहचान  बनी  रहे  ?  \n \nश्री  मती  अिम्बका  सोनी  : सभाप�त  महोदय , म�  माननीय  \nसदस्य  को   बताना  चाहती  हूं  �क  कोई